# Tag PPS devices for systemd, so dev-pps0.device exists (coordinator#11).
#
# systemd's own 99-systemd.rules tags block, net, tty, ptp, bluetooth, sound, usb, udc,
# backlight and misc/rfkill -- not pps. Without a tag udev never tells systemd the device
# is there, so `dev-pps0.device` NEVER ACTIVATES however long anything waits for it: a
# unit ordered After= it waits out DefaultDeviceTimeoutSec (90 s) and then fails with
# 'dependency'. That was coord-pps-log on every campod boot, and the 90 s was most of a
# pod's 1min 41s userspace boot.
#
# ptp being tagged upstream and pps not is a choice about which subsystems systemd
# promises units for, not a statement that a pps device is unfit to depend on. The tag is
# all that is missing; nothing else about the device needs changing.
#
# Verifiable on a device:
#   udevadm info /dev/pps0 | grep TAGS        the tag, as udev sees it
#   systemctl status dev-pps0.device          the unit it makes possible
SUBSYSTEM=="pps", TAG+="systemd"
